<title>DENMARK: Novo Nordisk, Boehringer sign r&amp;d pact.</title>
<headline>Novo Nordisk, Boehringer sign r&amp;d pact.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish biotech group Novo Nordisk said on Thursday that it had signed a research agreement with Germany's Boehringer Ingelheim aimed at seeking new treatments for obestity.</p>
<p>A Novo statement said that the multi-year pact would focus on new drugs, working through the the brain or fat cells to regulate food intake, energy expenditure or the number of fat cells.</p>
<p>Novo, the world's biggest insulin manuacturer, said that obesity was a major factor behind type two diabetes. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
